cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Radar Pulse Classification with Deep Learning
message: >-
  If you use this software or its results, please cite it using
  the metadata from this file.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Kaan Emre
    family-names: Evci
repository-code: "https://github.com/Adrift21/radar-pulse-classification"
abstract: >-
  Deep-learning classification of eight radar pulse waveform families from their
  time-frequency representations, with a focus on robustness under low signal-to-noise
  ratio conditions. Three time-frequency representations (STFT, Choi-Williams, and
  Wigner-Ville distributions) are compared across three architectures (a compact custom
  CNN, ResNet-50, and ViT-Small) on an identical frozen split spanning -10 dB to +20 dB.
keywords:
  - radar signal classification
  - time-frequency analysis
  - Wigner-Ville distribution
  - Choi-Williams distribution
  - deep learning
  - electronic warfare
  - SNR robustness
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-07-14"
